{TEXT("敌军保留预备队，并对已发现的暴露枪位呼叫炮火。进攻间隔较短，要及时转移和增援。"),TEXT("The enemy keeps reserves and calls artillery on observed, exposed gun posts. Shorter attack intervals demand timely movement and reinforcement."),TEXT("敌军保留预备队，记住暴露枪位，并配合炮火推进。敌我使用相同的武器与伤亡规则。")},
{TEXT("敌军保留预备队，并对已发现的暴露枪位呼叫炮火。进攻间隔较短，要及时转移和增援。"),TEXT("The enemy keeps reserves and calls artillery on observed, exposed gun posts. Shorter attack intervals demand timely movement and reinforcement."),TEXT("敌军保留预备队，以机枪和炮火支援反击。暴露的枪位会招来炮击。")},
{TEXT("敌军保留预备队，并对已发现的暴露枪位呼叫炮火。进攻间隔较短，要及时转移和增援。"),TEXT("The enemy keeps reserves and calls artillery on observed, exposed gun posts. Shorter attack intervals demand timely movement and reinforcement."),TEXT("The enemy holds reserves and supports counterattacks with machine guns and artillery. Exposed weapons draw shellfire.")},
{TEXT("敌军保留预备队，并对已发现的暴露枪位呼叫炮火。进攻间隔较短，要及时转移和增援。"),TEXT("The enemy keeps reserves and calls artillery on observed, exposed gun posts. Shorter attack intervals demand timely movement and reinforcement."),TEXT("The enemy keeps reserves, remembers exposed guns and coordinates its advance with artillery. Both sides use the same weapon and casualty rules.")},
{TEXT("敌军保留预备队，并对已发现的暴露枪位呼叫炮火。进攻间隔较短，要及时转移和增援。"),TEXT("The enemy keeps reserves and calls artillery on observed, exposed gun posts. Shorter attack intervals demand timely movement and reinforcement."),TEXT("敌军善于保留预备队、记住暴露的枪位，并让炮火与步兵互相掩护。每一次停留与出壕都需要判断；敌我仍遵守相同的命中、遮蔽和伤亡规则。")},
{TEXT("敌军更快投入后续梯队，利用烟幕和炮火掩护推进。分队之间需要相互支援。"),TEXT("The enemy brings follow-up waves sooner and advances under smoke and artillery. Keep sections within supporting distance."),TEXT("敌军更快组织下一梯队，按观察到的火力与兵力选择炮击地段。烟幕与机枪交替掩护，给孤立部队留下的喘息更少。")},
{TEXT("敌军更快投入后续梯队，利用烟幕和炮火掩护推进。分队之间需要相互支援。"),TEXT("The enemy brings follow-up waves sooner and advances under smoke and artillery. Keep sections within supporting distance."),TEXT("敌军接连投入后续梯队，以烟幕和炮火掩护推进。孤立的分队容易遭到围击。")},
{TEXT("敌军更快投入后续梯队，利用烟幕和炮火掩护推进。分队之间需要相互支援。"),TEXT("The enemy brings follow-up waves sooner and advances under smoke and artillery. Keep sections within supporting distance."),TEXT("Follow-up waves arrive in close succession, advancing under smoke and artillery. Isolated sections are vulnerable.")},
{TEXT("敌军更快投入后续梯队，利用烟幕和炮火掩护推进。分队之间需要相互支援。"),TEXT("The enemy brings follow-up waves sooner and advances under smoke and artillery. Keep sections within supporting distance."),TEXT("The enemy organises follow-up waves sooner and selects fire missions from observed troops and weapons. Smoke and machineguns provide alternating cover, leaving isolated units less time to recover.")},
{TEXT("敌军进攻间隔较长，部队有更多时间整队和等待增援。"),TEXT("Longer intervals between enemy attacks give more time to regroup and await reinforcements."),TEXT("敌军传令较慢，两次进攻之间有更多整队时间。适合熟悉战壕与支援。")},
{TEXT("敌军进攻间隔较长，部队有更多时间整队和等待增援。"),TEXT("Longer intervals between enemy attacks give more time to regroup and await reinforcements."),TEXT("敌军攻势较缓，进攻之间有较长的整队时间。")},
{TEXT("敌军进攻间隔较长，部队有更多时间整队和等待增援。"),TEXT("Longer intervals between enemy attacks give more time to regroup and await reinforcements."),TEXT("Enemy attacks are less frequent, allowing more time to regroup.")},
{TEXT("敌军进攻间隔较长，部队有更多时间整队和等待增援。"),TEXT("Longer intervals between enemy attacks give more time to regroup and await reinforcements."),TEXT("Enemy orders travel more slowly, leaving more time to regroup between attacks. A gentler introduction to trenches and support.")},
{TEXT("敌军进攻间隔较长，部队有更多时间整队和等待增援。"),TEXT("Longer intervals between enemy attacks give more time to regroup and await reinforcements."),TEXT("接近原有战役节奏。敌军传令较慢，进攻之间留有整队的间隙，适合熟悉战壕、火力与增援时机。")},
{TEXT("峰值亮度：%.0f nit。\n\n以显示器或 Windows HDR 校准结果为起点，调整到亮块中的十字刚好消失。若屏幕持续保留十字，使用已校准的峰值。\n\n范围：200–4000 nit。步进：50 nit。"),TEXT("Peak luminance: %.0f nits.\n\nStart with your display or Windows HDR calibration value. Adjust until the cross in the bright patch just disappears. If the display keeps the cross visible, retain its calibrated peak.\n\nRange: 200–4000 nits. Step: 50 nits."),TEXT("当前 %.0f nit，是游戏最亮高光的显示目标。1 nit = 1 cd/m²。\n\n保持平时的屏幕亮度和局部调光设置，以显示器或系统 HDR 校准的峰值起步。左侧亮块的十字比背景暗 10%%；逐步调到十字刚好消失。若始终可见，屏幕可能在映射亮部，请沿用已校准的峰值，不必一直推高。\n\n200–4000 nit；每次调整 50 nit。")},
{TEXT("峰值亮度：%.0f nit。\n\n以显示器或 Windows HDR 校准结果为起点，调整到亮块中的十字刚好消失。若屏幕持续保留十字，使用已校准的峰值。\n\n范围：200–4000 nit。步进：50 nit。"),TEXT("Peak luminance: %.0f nits.\n\nStart with your display or Windows HDR calibration value. Adjust until the cross in the bright patch just disappears. If the display keeps the cross visible, retain its calibrated peak.\n\nRange: 200–4000 nits. Step: 50 nits."),TEXT("Currently %.0f nits: the target for the brightest highlights. 1 nit = 1 cd/m².\n\nKeep your usual display brightness and local dimming. Start with the peak established by your display or Windows HDR calibration. The cross in the bright patch is 10%% darker than its background; adjust until it just disappears. If it stays visible, your display may be tone-mapping highlights. Keep the calibrated peak instead of raising it indefinitely.\n\n200–4000 nits; 50-nit steps.")},
{TEXT("纸白亮度：%.0f nit。%s\n\n控制普通白色与漫反射表面的亮度。调至白色舒适、十字清晰可辨。\n\n自动值跟随当前屏幕的 Windows 白亮度；无可用数据时为 203 nit。手动值按屏幕保存。\n\n范围：80–1000 nit，上限为屏幕峰值的 80%%。步进：10 nit。"),TEXT("Paper white: %.0f nits. %s\n\nSets the brightness of ordinary white and diffuse surfaces. Choose a comfortable white with the cross clearly visible.\n\nAutomatic values follow Windows white luminance for this display, or 203 nits when unavailable. Manual settings are saved per display.\n\nRange: 80–1000 nits, capped at 80%% of display peak. Step: 10 nits."),TEXT("当前 %.0f nit，决定普通白色和漫反射物体的亮度基准，不是火光的最高亮度。%s\n\n默认跟随当前屏幕的 Windows 白亮度，无法读取时使用 203 nit。峰值亮度不能代替纸白。手动调整后会为这块屏幕保留，恢复推荐值可再次跟随系统。\n\n白色应自然舒适，块内十字应能分辨，不要以让它消失为目标。80–1000 nit，最高为屏幕峰值的 80%%；每次调整 10 nit。")},
{TEXT("纸白亮度：%.0f nit。%s\n\n控制普通白色与漫反射表面的亮度。调至白色舒适、十字清晰可辨。\n\n自动值跟随当前屏幕的 Windows 白亮度；无可用数据时为 203 nit。手动值按屏幕保存。\n\n范围：80–1000 nit，上限为屏幕峰值的 80%%。步进：10 nit。"),TEXT("Paper white: %.0f nits. %s\n\nSets the brightness of ordinary white and diffuse surfaces. Choose a comfortable white with the cross clearly visible.\n\nAutomatic values follow Windows white luminance for this display, or 203 nits when unavailable. Manual settings are saved per display.\n\nRange: 80–1000 nits, capped at 80%% of display peak. Step: 10 nits."),TEXT("Currently %.0f nits: the reference brightness for ordinary white and diffuse surfaces, not the peak of flames. %s\n\nAutomatic mode follows this display's Windows white level, using 203 nits when unavailable. Peak brightness cannot replace paper white. Manual values are remembered for each display; restore recommendations to follow Windows again.\n\nWhite should look natural and comfortable, with the cross still distinguishable. Do not try to make it disappear. 80–1000 nits, limited to 80%% of display peak; 10-nit steps.")},
{TEXT("跟随 Windows 设置。"),TEXT("Following Windows settings."),TEXT("目前自动跟随系统。")},
{TEXT("跟随 Windows 设置。"),TEXT("Following Windows settings."),TEXT("Currently following Windows automatically.")},
{TEXT("手动校准。"),TEXT("Manual calibration."),TEXT("目前使用手动校准。")},
{TEXT("手动校准。"),TEXT("Manual calibration."),TEXT("Currently using manual calibration.")},
{TEXT("界面亮度：%.0f nit。%s\n\n控制文字、照片和操作台的亮度。调至文字清楚、亮边柔和。战场曝光保持不变。\n\n自动值跟随当前屏幕的 Windows 白亮度；无可用数据时为 203 nit。手动值按屏幕保存。\n\n范围：80–1000 nit，上限为屏幕峰值的 80%%。步进：10 nit。"),TEXT("Interface luminance: %.0f nits. %s\n\nSets the brightness of text, photographs and the console. Keep lettering clear and bright edges comfortable. Battlefield exposure is unchanged.\n\nAutomatic values follow Windows white luminance, or 203 nits when unavailable. Manual settings are saved per display.\n\nRange: 80–1000 nits, capped at 80%% of display peak. Step: 10 nits."),TEXT("当前 %.0f nit，单独控制文字、照片和操作台的亮度；不改变战场曝光或高光峰值。%s\n\n默认跟随当前屏幕的 Windows 白亮度，读取失败时使用 203 nit。先把画面纸白调舒服，再看本页文字与战场操作台。降低刺眼的字和亮边，提高到文字清楚即可。\n\n每块屏幕独立保留手动值。80–1000 nit，最高为屏幕峰值的 80%%；每次调整 10 nit。")},
{TEXT("界面亮度：%.0f nit。%s\n\n控制文字、照片和操作台的亮度。调至文字清楚、亮边柔和。战场曝光保持不变。\n\n自动值跟随当前屏幕的 Windows 白亮度；无可用数据时为 203 nit。手动值按屏幕保存。\n\n范围：80–1000 nit，上限为屏幕峰值的 80%%。步进：10 nit。"),TEXT("Interface luminance: %.0f nits. %s\n\nSets the brightness of text, photographs and the console. Keep lettering clear and bright edges comfortable. Battlefield exposure is unchanged.\n\nAutomatic values follow Windows white luminance, or 203 nits when unavailable. Manual settings are saved per display.\n\nRange: 80–1000 nits, capped at 80%% of display peak. Step: 10 nits."),TEXT("Currently %.0f nits: the separate brightness of text, photographs and the console. It does not change battlefield exposure or peak highlights. %s\n\nAutomatic mode follows this display's Windows white level, using 203 nits when unavailable. Set comfortable paper white first, then judge the text here and the battlefield console. Reduce glare while keeping the lettering clear.\n\nManual values are saved per display. 80–1000 nits, limited to 80%% of display peak; 10-nit steps.")},
{TEXT("参照块：%.4f nit。十字：%.4f nit。\n\n用于检查近黑层次。十字应隐约可辨；室内反光会影响判断。此项仅调整参照图。\n\n范围：0.0001–0.1 nit。每步减半或加倍。"),TEXT("Reference patch: %.4f nits. Cross: %.4f nits.\n\nChecks near-black detail. The cross should be faintly visible; room reflections affect this test. This control adjusts the reference patch only.\n\nRange: 0.0001–0.1 nits. Each step halves or doubles the value."),TEXT("右侧参照块为 %.4f nit，十字为 %.4f nit。它只用来观察屏幕的近黑层次，不改变战场曝光或黑位。\n\n从接近纯黑开始，看十字是否仍能辨认。若暗部被室内反光盖住，先调整环境；不要用这个参照去抬亮整幅游戏。\n\n0.0001–0.1 nit；每次减半或加倍。")},
{TEXT("参照块：%.4f nit。十字：%.4f nit。\n\n用于检查近黑层次。十字应隐约可辨；室内反光会影响判断。此项仅调整参照图。\n\n范围：0.0001–0.1 nit。每步减半或加倍。"),TEXT("Reference patch: %.4f nits. Cross: %.4f nits.\n\nChecks near-black detail. The cross should be faintly visible; room reflections affect this test. This control adjusts the reference patch only.\n\nRange: 0.0001–0.1 nits. Each step halves or doubles the value."),TEXT("The reference patch is %.4f nits; its cross is %.4f nits. This only reveals near-black detail and does not alter battlefield exposure or black level.\n\nStart near black and check whether the cross remains distinguishable. If room reflections obscure it, adjust the viewing environment first. Do not use this reference to brighten the whole game.\n\n0.0001–0.1 nits; each step halves or doubles the value.")},
{TEXT("细微胶片颗粒，为战场增添旧式摄影的质感。"),TEXT("Fine film grain adds the texture of period photography to the battlefield."),TEXT("细微的明暗颗粒保留战地胶片质感，只作用于战场，不覆盖界面文字。")},
{TEXT("细微胶片颗粒，为战场增添旧式摄影的质感。"),TEXT("Fine film grain adds the texture of period photography to the battlefield."),TEXT("Subtle luminance grain lends the battlefield a period-film texture without covering interface text.")},
{TEXT("烟幕掩护部队穿过开阔地、转移枪位。浓烟遮蔽双方视线，炮弹仍可穿过。"),TEXT("Smoke covers open-ground crossings and changes of position. It obscures both armies; shells can still pass through."),TEXT("提前指定转移路线上的遮蔽地段。等烟幕铺开再推进；机枪手也会失去穿烟观察，别误以为只有敌人看不见。")},
{TEXT("烟幕掩护部队穿过开阔地、转移枪位。浓烟遮蔽双方视线，炮弹仍可穿过。"),TEXT("Smoke covers open-ground crossings and changes of position. It obscures both armies; shells can still pass through."),TEXT("Select a screening area along your intended route before moving. Wait for the smoke to spread. Your own machine gunners also lose observation through it; the screen does not blind only the enemy.")},
{TEXT("炮火覆盖指定地段，抵达前留有传令与装定时间。弹着区内的友军同样会受伤。"),TEXT("Fire covers the selected ground after the order is relayed and the guns are laid. Friendly troops in the target area are also at risk."),TEXT("先观察敌军，再指定覆盖地段。支援需要时间抵达；落点确认后，及时让己方部队避开危险区域。")},
{TEXT("炮火覆盖指定地段，抵达前留有传令与装定时间。弹着区内的友军同样会受伤。"),TEXT("Fire covers the selected ground after the order is relayed and the guns are laid. Friendly troops in the target area are also at risk."),TEXT("Observe the enemy before selecting the area. Support takes time to arrive. Once the target is confirmed, move friendly troops away from the danger.")},
{TEXT("战车从后方进入。履带与机枪可被分别击毁；步兵能掩护车侧，工兵可抢修受损部件。"),TEXT("Tanks enter from the rear. Tracks and machine guns can be disabled separately. Infantry cover the flanks; pioneers can repair damaged components."),TEXT("车组从后方沿通路推进。履带受损会影响行进，机枪也可能失去作用；不要把战车单独送进敌方炮火。")},
{TEXT("战车从后方进入。履带与机枪可被分别击毁；步兵能掩护车侧，工兵可抢修受损部件。"),TEXT("Tanks enter from the rear. Tracks and machine guns can be disabled separately. Infantry cover the flanks; pioneers can repair damaged components."),TEXT("The crew approaches along a route from the rear. Damaged tracks hinder movement and machine guns can be disabled separately. Do not send a tank alone into enemy gunfire.")},
{TEXT("战术要点"),TEXT("Field notes"),TEXT("军士的叮嘱")},
{TEXT("战术要点"),TEXT("Field notes"),TEXT("The sergeant's advice")},
{TEXT("准备出发"),TEXT("Ready to move"),TEXT("明白，准备出发")},
{TEXT("准备出发"),TEXT("Ready to move"),TEXT("Understood. Ready to move")},
{TEXT("该编制尚未配属。"),TEXT("This formation is not yet assigned."),TEXT("编制不可用")},
{TEXT("该编制尚未配属。"),TEXT("This formation is not yet assigned."),TEXT("This formation is unavailable")},
{TEXT("更改立即生效。"),TEXT("Changes apply immediately."),TEXT("更改立即生效并保存。")},
{TEXT("更改立即生效。"),TEXT("Changes apply immediately."),TEXT("Changes apply and save immediately.")},
{TEXT("更改立即生效。"),TEXT("Changes apply immediately."),TEXT("更改立即生效；此偏好与战役及显示设置分别保存。")},
{TEXT("先完成防毒训练并配发面具，再进入毒气区。烟幕无法阻隔毒气。"),TEXT("Respirator training and equipment are required before entering gas. Smoke provides no protection."),TEXT("进入毒气前先研习并配发防毒面具；烟幕不能隔绝毒气。")},
{TEXT("先完成防毒训练并配发面具，再进入毒气区。烟幕无法阻隔毒气。"),TEXT("Respirator training and equipment are required before entering gas. Smoke provides no protection."),TEXT("Research respirators before entering gas; a smoke screen provides no protection from gas.")},
{TEXT("删除所选的 %d 份战役档案，包括研究与进度。删除后无法恢复。"),TEXT("Delete the selected %d campaign records, including research and progress. This cannot be undone."),TEXT("将删除所选的 %d 条战役及其研究和进度。此操作无法在游戏中撤销。")},
{TEXT("删除所选的 %d 份战役档案，包括研究与进度。删除后无法恢复。"),TEXT("Delete the selected %d campaign records, including research and progress. This cannot be undone."),TEXT("The selected %d campaigns, their research and progress will be deleted. This cannot be undone in the game.")},
{TEXT("友军误伤、毒气和近距离敌方装甲会削弱士气。占领战壕、推进和部队相互支援可恢复少量士气。"),TEXT("Friendly fire, gas and nearby enemy armour reduce morale. Capturing trenches, advancing and mutual support restore a little."),TEXT("友军误伤、毒气和近距离装甲威胁会动摇士气。攻下战壕、稳步推进，以及互相支援的部队会少量恢复信心。")},
